    "remaining_open_items": [
      "Package-terminal ordering differs from a simple geometric CCW assumption; bind explicitly.",
      "Leakage, common-mode saturation and fitted HF loss remain unresolved.",
      "Former simulation blocker resolved for the explicitly bound reference (2026-10-08): Mains-rated winding binding and missing saturation/thermal model need explicit handling; insulation test voltage is not a working voltage. Resolution: Proposed explicit handling: a DC winding-resistance-only, op-only binding that makes no mains, insulation or isolation claim, with no saturation or thermal model. The 250 V AC 50 Hz rated voltage is kept as a sourced rating to enforce, and the 1500 V AC / 2 s figure is recorded only as a test voltage. Because tran is not supported, no mains-frequency simulation can run on it. Pin binding: the WE datasheet (744821240 rev 004.000, archived sha 87ca9b97...) schematic gives windings 1->4 and 2->3 with dots at 1 and 2. Its top view puts 1 and 2 10.0 mm apart and 1 and 4 4.5 mm apart, while spec line 3487 puts package 1-2 4.5 mm apart (x = -5) and 1-4 10 mm apart. With pin 1 held fixed, manufacturer->package is {1:1, 2:4, 3:3, 4:2}, so the windings are package 1-2 and 4-3, dotted at package 1 and 4. The spec's adopted default (A1=1, A2=4, B1=2, B2=3) pairs pins across the 10 mm span in package numbering and is wrong. If the caller wants mains entries kept blocked as policy, this entry should stay blocked; the evidence for the DC binding itself is complete.",
      "Leakage inductance, CM saturation and HF loss (not in the datasheet)",
      "Any mains/safety acceptance (out of scope; never claimed)",
      "Thermal model for the 70 C / <55 K rating"
